# Kerrigan outpoint/address freeze list -- incident 2026-05
#
# Defensive, opt-in, REVERSIBLE. Loaded via:
#   -blacklistoutpoints=/path/to/incident-2026-05.blacklist
#
# A node running with this list will REFUSE TO RELAY (mempool) and REFUSE TO
# MINE (block template) any transaction that spends a listed outpoint, or any
# output paying a listed address. This is Layer 1 (relay/policy) only: it does
# NOT split the chain. If a supermajority of pool hashpower runs it, the
# thief's onward spends -- including any transparent->Sapling shield -- cannot
# confirm.
#
# It does NOT move, seize, or redirect funds and touches no key material.
#
# FORMAT (one entry per line):
#   <txid>:<vout>     freeze a specific outpoint (most precise)
#   <address>         freeze every output paying this address
#   # ...             comment (whole-line or trailing); blank lines ignored
#
# TO REMOVE an entry later (un-freeze): delete the line (or the whole option)
# and restart the daemon. No on-disk consensus state is created by Layer 1.
#
# Source of these entries: red-swarm fund trace (A-fund-trace.md), Kerrigan
# MAINNET, theft confirmed in block 54351 (2026-05-27 20:35:59 UTC). The drain
# address is empty (funds moved); these are the live resting points + the most
# precise known peel-chain outpoints.

